{"title":"Mediant theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>Not to be confused with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Median\" title=\"Median\">median</a>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mediant_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <b>mediant</b> of two fractions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8362dd17da7c07cedd4018d589a0b21e9575e287.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8a641d7f000ac0d1e38930dd61c491c1581bcd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> is defined as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e06ae28109e1099a976da9a28d4bb82e42c1a186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+b}{c+d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"45\" height=\"41\" /> for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c8779302abff1994607b10c65875dae12faefbdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d  (b\\ne 0, d\\ne 0, b+d\\ne 0).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"253\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The <b>Mediant theorem</b> states that for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84c280c55827089f2865285848622c8163af44d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, a_2, ... ,a_n, b_1, b_2, ... ,b_n (b_i\\ne 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"250\" height=\"20\" />,\n</p><p><br />\nif <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2ca36af4d9c7f2c69f0c4bd2f43c34fb41d43860.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1}{b_1} = \\frac{a_2}{b_2} = ... = \\frac{a_n}{b_n},\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"35\" /> then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/8/c78b610d98f5ed891a0b8b2e4e2f3f4fc1e4971e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1}{b_1} = \\frac{a_2}{b_2} = ... = \\frac{a_n}{b_n} = \\frac{a_1+a_2+...+a_n}{b_1+b_2+...+b_n}.\\]\" width=\"317\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mediant_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/f/d3fcf3cc8878fc1dcf56a8a20dc8878b1a06e2bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1}{b_1} = \\frac{a_2}{b_2} = ... = \\frac{a_n}{b_n} = k.\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/38631c58580bbeb2fca92be04c6bea21eda87b01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i = kb_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/2858ceec9eda628e1db2727b5eddd7d9fcfa5d95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1+a_2+...+a_n}{b_1+b_2+...+b_n}=\\frac{k(b_1+b_2+...+b_n)}{b_1+b_2+...+b_n}=k. \\quad \\blacksquare\\]\" width=\"387\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Expansion\">Expansion</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mediant_theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Expansion\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Furthermore, for nonzero real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/5/83538d40711b5afca880344ae850b1d07489e864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1,x_2,...,x_n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><br />\nif <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/a/2ca36af4d9c7f2c69f0c4bd2f43c34fb41d43860.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1}{b_1} = \\frac{a_2}{b_2} = ... = \\frac{a_n}{b_n},\\]\" width=\"154\" height=\"35\" /> then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25ed8fb86b6b1ec31aad1723df1c568c8b9c1b92.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a_1}{b_1} = \\frac{a_2}{b_2} = ... = \\frac{a_n}{b_n} = \\frac{a_1x_1+a_2x_2+...+a_nx_n}{b_1x_1+b_2x_2+...+b_nx_n}.\\]\" width=\"372\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThis can also be proved easily by letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e5017fb167ffb7542f2481f431c42ea8b6b54efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a_1}{b_1} = \\frac{a_2}{b_2} = ... = \\frac{a_n}{b_n} = k.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"194\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202950\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 72/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2984/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:25898:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202950 and revision id 205830. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}